Created: 08 FEB 2023

	Last modified:

    26 AUG 2025:
    Replaced all files as a result of updating my Ramses fork and patches in response to the significant changes made to the main Ramses repo. See TTG_README in my fork's main dir.
    Added detail information about the modifications needed to merge my dice patch with oagertz.
    TESTING in progress with model
        fgas10_agama_rf
        hbd_10_gd11_s4_star_tag

	15 JAN 2024:
	Changes to read_params.f90 in response to changes to some files one level up (see corresponding change log in ../README)

	01 FEB 2024:
	Remove init_refine.f90 because it is redundant with the same file in patch/tepper/dice.

	15 FEB 2024:
	init_flow_fine.f90: Enclose 'if(metal)' statements within 'if(star.or.sink)' statement, consistent with other subroutines, to avoid segmentation fault when eps_star = 0. SEE "IMPORTANT 1)" below

	28 FEB 2024:
	Added family tag, previously set to 0 by default, now set to the value specified by the ICs (if available)

	06 MAR 2024:
	Introduced two new DICE input parameters, ic_scale_metalO/Fe, to weigh the O/Fe initial abundance ratios (previously hard-coded to a value of 0.333)

About:

This subdirectory contains a number of patches to files originally in /Users/tepper/codes/ramses_fork/patch/init/dice/.

The modifications are intended to make this patch work with /Users/tepper/codes/ramses_fork/patch/tepper/oagertz/.

The necessary modifications have been accomplished by:
	1) Copying to this directory *all* the file in /Users/tepper/codes/ramses_fork/patch/init/dice/.
	2) Comparing with FileMerge the files *common* to the two above directories (add_list.f90, init_part.f90, particle_tree.f90), and adding the required code snippets
	3) Some files needed to be additionally edited by hand:
		- init_part.f90: make the zp array consistent with nmetals, i.e. 2D
        - init_flow_fine.f90: make the metallicity initialisation consistent with nmetals, i.e. 2D, accounting for the variables ic_scale_metalO and ic_scale_metalFe


Notes:
	- Some modifications are flagged by 'ERIC', 'EDGE2', or 'TTG', but not all
	- See also:
		/Users/tepper/codes/ramses_agertz/ramses/patch/dice/README

IMPORTANT:

	1) These patches do not split all if-clauses of the form:

		if(star.or.sink)then
			if(metal)then
			endif
		endif
	into:
		if(star.or.sink)then
			...
		endif
		if(metal)then
			...
		endif

	as does my dice patch in, e.g. particle_tree.f90.

	2) From Tine Colman related to init_flow_fine.f90

	    "! TC: this file should now be compatible with MHD, but I didn't test it."



-----------------------------------------
MODIFIED FILES AND MODIFICATIONS
* Note that not all modifications are detailed as they are, but they can be easily searched for with the information provided

    add_list.f90
    12 relevant difference(s) with respect to my patched dice version
    To subroutines add_free() and add_free_cond()
    - added
        use hydro_parameters,only: nmetals
    - added
        integer:: imet ! ERIC
    - added initialisation
        mpb(ind_part(j))=0.0  !EDGE2
    - added initialisation
        zp(ind_part(j),imet)=0.0
    - added blocks starting with
        if (dice_init)


    init_part.f90:
    14 relevant difference(s) with respect to my patched dice version
    - all if-clauses of the form:
        if(star.or.sink)then
            ...
        endif
        if(metal)then
        endif
    nested into:
        if(star.or.sink)then
            if(metal)then
            endif
        endif
    - added
        use hydro_parameters,only: nmetals ! ERIC
    - added
        integer :: imet ! ERIC
    - added allocation
        allocate(itmpp (npartmax))
    - added allocation / initialisation
        allocate(mpb(npartmax))
        mpb=0.0
    - added allocation / initialisation
        allocate(zp(npartmax,nmetals)) ! ERIC
        zp=0.0
    - added read
        zp(1:npart2,imet)=xdp
    - added read
        mpb(1:npart2)=xdp
    - added initialisation
        zp(ipart,imet)=0d0
    - modified assignment of metallicity
    ! zp(ipart)  = zz(i)
        zp(ipart,1)  = ic_scale_metalFe * zz(i) !Iron
        zp(ipart,2)  = ic_scale_metalO  * zz(i) !Oxygen
    and
        zp(ipart+1,1:nmetals)  = z_ave*0.02 ! TTG
    where relevant


    - init_flow_fine.f90:
    8 relevant difference(s) with respect to my patched dice version
    - replaced in init_uold()
        if(metal) then
          if(ivar.eq.imetal) uold(active(ilevel)%igrid(i)+iskip,ivar) = max(IG_rho/scale_nH,smallr)*IG_metal*ic_scale_metal
        endif
    by
        if(star.or.sink)then
           ! ERIC
           if(metal) then
             ! Iron
             if(ivar.eq.imetal) &
             & uold(active(ilevel)%igrid(i)+iskip,ivar) = &
             & ic_scale_metalFe * max(IG_rho/scale_nH,smallr) * IG_metal * ic_scale_metal
             ! Oxygen
             if(ivar.eq.imetal+1) &
             & uold(active(ilevel)%igrid(i)+iskip,ivar) = &
             & ic_scale_metalO * max(IG_rho/scale_nH,smallr) * IG_metal * ic_scale_metal
           endif
        endif
    - added to surbroutine init_gas_cic()
        integer:: imet ! ERIC
    - replaced in soubroutine init_gas_cic()
        if(metal) then
          uold(indp(j,ind),imetal)=uold(indp(j,ind),imetal)+mp(ind_part(j))*vol(j,ind)/vol_loc(j)*zp(ind_part(j))
        endif
    by
        if(star.or.sink)then
           if(metal) then
              ! ERIC
              do imet=1,nmetals
                 uold(indp(j,ind),imetal+imet-1) = uold(indp(j,ind),imetal+imet-1) + mp(ind_part(j))*vol(j,ind)/vol_loc(j)*zp(ind_part(j),imet)
              enddo
           endif
        endif
    - added in subroutine init_gas_ngp()
        integer:: imet ! ERIC
    - replaced in subroutine init_gas_ngp()
        if(metal) then
           uold(indp(j),imetal)=uold(indp(j),imetal)+mp(ind_part(j))/vol_loc(j)*zp(ind_part(j))
        endif
    by
        if(star.or.sink)then
           if(metal) then
           ! ERIC
              do imet=1,nmetals
                  uold(indp(j),imetal+imet-1) = uold(indp(j),imetal+imet+1) + mp(ind_part(j))/vol_loc(j)*zp(ind_part(j),imet)
              enddo
           endif
        endif


    - particle_tree.f90
    11 relevant difference(s) with respect to my patched dice version
    - added to subroutine virtual_tree_fine()
        use hydro_parameters,only: nmetals ! ERIC
    - replaced
        if(star.or.sink) then
            particle_data_width=twondim+2
        endif
        if(metal) then
           particle_data_width=twondim+3
        endif
    by
        if(star.or.sink) then
